reims-vgpu: the sampled cache's content digest is a four-lane multiply hash.

find_cached_sampled hashes an incoming sampled blob on every bind that misses
the identity path, and admission hashes each retained one. The digest was two
salted SipHash-1-3 passes. It only narrows the walk to one candidate: the
retained bytes beside each entry are compared, and that compare decides every
hit and every deduplication (ResidentSampledSlot::content). A recorded busy
app second on the development host: 418 buffer-texture binds, every one a
content hit over 843 MB (sampled_cache_hits, sampled_cache_hit_bytes), and
draw_phase acquire_sampled_us 305 ms.

Now sampled_content_hash is four independent lanes of XXH64's round over
32-byte stripes, the tail spread over the lanes, folded into two 64-bit halves
with different multipliers and each finished with XXH64's avalanche, the length
in both. A collision costs one failed compare, never a wrong image, so the
digest needs mixing, not cryptographic strength. The stale doc comment that
still said the digest decided alone is corrected.

Offline (content_hash_timing, one 2 MB blob): the two SipHash passes 544-549
us, the new digest 91-92 us, the deciding memcmp 57-58 us (medians of 31).
Not measured on a live phone.

--- a/reims-vgpu/crates/reims-vgpu/src/backend/vulkan/engine/pools/mod.rs
